From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ARM: dts: gts28ltexx: Bluetooth at 3 Mbaud, UART3 on the
 audio PLL

The BCM4358 ran at 460800 baud because UART3's clock, sclk_aud_uart,
came from the oscillator: the bootloader leaves CMU_AUD's
mout_aud_pll_user on the 24 MHz oscclk, and 921600 needs a zero UBRDIV,
after which the controller stopped answering.  460800 baud carries
46 kB/s; A2DP's high quality SBC takes 41 kB/s before its framing, and
SBC-XQ more than the link has.

Move mout_aud_pll_user to the audio PLL, as TM2 does
(exynos5433-tm2-common.dtsi), give sclk_aud_uart the PLL's 196.6 MHz
undivided, and run the controller at 3 Mbaud, TM2's speed on the same
UART.  The driver rounds the divider down to UBRDIV 3 and UFRACVAL 1:
3.025 Mbaud, 0.8 % fast.

The PLL feeds the whole audio block, so its other dividers go to 8: the
audio bus, the CA5 and the I2S, PCM and SLIMbus clocks run at 24.6 MHz
instead of 24 MHz.  The WM1814 is the I2S clock provider, from its own
MCLK (the PMU's CLKOUT), and I2S0 runs on its bus clock
(gts28_wm1814.c: CBP_CFP, SAMSUNG_I2S_OPCLK_PCLK), so playback and
capture do not depend on these rates.  On the tablet: firmware 0144
loads, a scan finds 16 devices, the UART counts no framing, parity or
overrun error, and 2 s of playback and 2.5 s of microphone capture
behave as before (same duration, the same two existing codec warnings).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-bt.dtsi | 44 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-bt.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-bt.dtsi
index 81e5f5b60..37581a6df 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-bt.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-bt.dtsi
@@ -109,16 +109,46 @@ bluetooth {
 		clock-names = "extclk";
 
 		/*
-		 * Stock runs 921600 (libbt_vndcfg.txt UART_TARGET_BAUD_RATE),
-		 * but UART3 is clocked at 24 MHz here (sclk_aud_uart from
-		 * oscclk), which gives UBRDIV = 0 at 921600: after the baud
-		 * switch the controller no longer answers (seen on the
-		 * device, 2026-10-28).  460800 gives UBRDIV = 2 (0.16 %
-		 * error) and works.
+		 * 3 Mbaud, as TM2 runs the same UART: sclk_aud_uart comes
+		 * from the audio PLL at 196.6 MHz (&cmu_aud below), and the
+		 * driver, which rounds the divider down, sets UBRDIV 3 and
+		 * UFRACVAL 1 (read back on the tablet): 3.025 Mbaud, 0.8 %
+		 * fast.  On the bootloader's 24 MHz oscclk the UART stopped
+		 * at 460800: 921600 needs UBRDIV = 0, after which the
+		 * controller no longer answered (2026-10-28), and 460800
+		 * baud carries 46 kB/s, which A2DP's high quality SBC
+		 * (41 kB/s before its framing) nearly fills and SBC-XQ
+		 * exceeds (2026-11-08).  The stock tree runs 921600
+		 * (libbt_vndcfg.txt UART_TARGET_BAUD_RATE).
 		 */
-		max-speed = <460800>;
+		max-speed = <3000000>;
 
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&bt_host_wake_pins &bt_wake_pins &bt_en_pins>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * UART3's baud clock, sclk_aud_uart, divides CMU_AUD's mout_aud_pll_user,
+ * which the bootloader leaves on oscclk: 24 MHz for the whole audio block.
+ * Move it to the audio PLL (fout_aud_pll, 196.6 MHz, already running) as
+ * TM2 does (exynos5433-tm2-common.dtsi &cmu_aud), give the UART the PLL
+ * undivided, and divide everything else by 8, to 24.6 MHz, so the audio
+ * block's bus, its debug clocks and the I2S, PCM and SLIMbus clocks stay
+ * close to the 24 MHz they ran at: the codec drives the I2S bit and frame
+ * clocks from its own MCLK (the PMU CLKOUT), and I2S0 only uses its bus
+ * clock (gts28_wm1814.c: CBP_CFP, SAMSUNG_I2S_OPCLK_PCLK).  The rates
+ * carry a few hertz of slack because the PLL runs at 196608009 Hz and a
+ * divider never goes above the rate it is asked for.
+ */
+&cmu_aud {
+	assigned-clocks = <&cmu_aud CLK_MOUT_AUD_PLL_USER>,
+			  <&cmu_aud CLK_DIV_AUD_CA5>,
+			  <&cmu_aud CLK_DIV_SCLK_AUD_I2S>,
+			  <&cmu_aud CLK_DIV_SCLK_AUD_PCM>,
+			  <&cmu_aud CLK_DIV_SCLK_AUD_SLIMBUS>,
+			  <&cmu_aud CLK_DIV_SCLK_AUD_UART>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&cmu_top CLK_FOUT_AUD_PLL>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <0>, <24576002>, <24576002>, <24576002>,
+			       <24576002>, <196608010>;
+};
